# Bernstein-agent runtime state (resolves the design decision raised in
# issue #2837).  `.sdd/` is the Bernstein agent-orchestration runtime —
# `attestations/`, `traces/`, `index/`, `memory/`, `agents/`, `routing/`,
# `caching/`, `backlog/`, `metrics/`, `upgrades/`, `auth/`, `archive/`,
# `default/`, `knowledge/file_index.json`, and `knowledge/decisions.jsonl`
# are all per-developer / per-session state (Ed25519 signatures, JSONL
# trace logs, SQLite codebase caches, agent catalog snapshots, etc.).
# The previous `.sdd/runtime/` ignore was the original intent — issue
# #2837 generalized it to the whole directory because:
#   1. The only "doc-like" file (`.sdd/knowledge/architecture.md`) is an
#      auto-generated file index from the Bernstein tool, not
#      human-authored documentation.  Its drift was the bug #2818/#2828
#      sweep had to fix, and a CI freshness gate would just re-create
#      the maintenance burden in a different place.
#   2. `.sdd/index/codebase.db` (26 MB) and the JSONL trace files are
#      genuinely per-machine session state and have no business in git.
#   3. Templates and scripts that reference `.sdd/` paths (e.g.
#      `templates/skills/bernstein-signal-check.md`,
#      `scripts/autonomous_parameter_sweep.py`) write runtime data and
#      do not depend on the files being tracked.
# Local agents and developers regenerate their `.sdd/` state on first run;
# no shared canonical view is lost because none existed — every Bernstein
# run rebuilt the index from scratch.
.sdd/

# Bernstein-agent auto-generated session file (per AGENTS.md line 218).
# The root `.md` policy gate (`scripts/check_root_md_policy.py`) only
# *warns* on this file; the `.gitignore` line is the real defense that
# prevents it from ever being staged.  See issue #2466.
CLAUDE.md

# Local agent / orchestrator runtime dirs (see AGENTS.md §Repository Hygiene).
# Issue #2954 added a CI gate (`scripts/check_root_hygiene.py`) that flags
# any dotfile/dotdir at repo root that is neither in
# `ROOT_DOTFILE_ALLOWLIST` nor matched by `.gitignore` nor already tracked
# in git. These entries are the matching `.gitignore` lines for each
# runtime dir the gate is supposed to accept on every fresh checkout.
# A handful of these dirs (`.automaker/`, `.jules/`, `.serena/`,
# `.sisyphus/`, `.superset/`, `.gitnexus/`, `.issues/`, `.agents/`)
# were committed historically and are still tracked; the gitignore line
# below is the real defense — it prevents NEW files from being staged on
# subsequent commits.
.agents/
.automaker/
.jules/
.serena/
.sisyphus/
.superset/
.gitnexus/
.issues/
.opencode/
.claude/

# Python testing framework caches (root-level `.hypothesis/` appeared in
# fresh checkouts and was flagged by the #2954 gate).
.hypothesis/

# ONNX model artifacts (issue #1335) — pinned via tests/surrogate_models/registry.json, never committed
*.onnx
# Test fixtures that escaped temp directories (see #2949). Stricter
# pattern than the blanket `*.onnx` above so the escapee is named
# explicitly in audit logs and the broader root-hygiene gate can refer
# back to a single grep-able symbol.
tests_tmp_*.onnx
# Models directory: ignore everything inside, then re-include specific
# tracked artifacts below. Issue #2923 manifest must be tracked so the
# surrogate drift gate can resolve mode=fallback honestly (the manifest's
# presence is the operator's explicit acknowledgement that fallback mode
# is acceptable for this milestone).
models/*
models/*.onnx
models/*.pt
models/*.pth
models/*.pkl
models/*.h5
# Issue #2923 fail-closed surrogate-gate manifest. Re-includes the `.sha256`
# sidecar after the blanket `models/*` ignore above. The `.sha256` file is
# the ONLY artifact in `models/` that is tracked; the `.onnx` itself stays
# gitignored. If a future manifest is added, copy the negation pattern below.
!models/surrogate_zone_thermal.onnx.sha256

# EPW/DDY weather files — fetched on demand from EnergyPlus/ASHRAE data portals.
# ASHRAE 140 validation requires real TMY3 weather files; run
# `python3 scripts/fetch_ashrae140_epw.py` to download before running the
# full ASHRAE 140 test suite.  See issue #N (tracking).
*.epw
*.ddy
assets/weather/*.epw
assets/weather/*.ddy
tests/test_data/*.epw
tests/test_data/*.ddy
tests/data/v0.4/weather/*.epw
tests/data/v0.4/weather/*.ddy
tests/data/v0.5/weather/*.epw
tests/data/v0.5/weather/*.ddy

